# openOODA Platform Capabilities & System Guarantees

This document serves as the single source of truth for all fully verified, shipped, and production-tested capabilities in the openOODA platform. Every system listed below is proven by end-to-end fixtures and smoke test suites across all compilation targets.

================================================================================
1. Core Language & Execution Model
================================================================================

  Native Compilation Pipeline
    - Direct C Code Emission: Compiles high-level `.oo` source into optimized ANSI C, linked with the lightweight `chs_rt` runtime and compiled to native machine code via GCC or Clang.
    - WebAssembly Backend (`oodac/wasm_emit_*.oo`): Emits spec-compliant WASM binary modules (`.wasm`) with structured linear memory, LEB128 encoding, and WASI host call bindings.
    - LLVM IR Backend (`oodac/llvm_emit_*.oo`): Emits typed LLVM Intermediate Representation with SSA form, explicit GEP pointer math, and ARC retain/release runtime shims.
    - Multi-Pass Type Checker: Strict type inference, pattern exhaustiveness checking, and type-state lifecycle validation.

  Safe Memory & Resource Lifecycle
    - Automatic Reference Counting (ARC): Deterministic memory deallocation when references drop, with zero stop-the-world pauses.
    - Linear & Affine Ownership: Enforces single-consumer tokens and move semantics for sensitive hardware resources.
    - Type-State Transitions (`std/src/ooda/typestate/`): Proves lifecycle states (e.g. `Unopened` -> `Opened` -> `Closed`) at compile time, eliminating invalid state access.
    - Compile-Time Refinement Solver (`std/src/ooda/proofs/`): Verifies `requires` and `ensures` function contracts statically with interval bounds and arithmetic verification.

================================================================================
2. Capability Security & Operating System Isolation
================================================================================

  Object-Capability Security Model (`std/src/ooda/sec/sys/objcap*.oo`)
    - Cryptographic Capability Seals: Unforgeable HMAC-SHA256 capability tokens required for all external, file, network, time, random, and memory operations.
    - Monotonic Rights Diminution: Enforces capability attenuation (`attenuate_rights`) where child tokens can only drop or retain permissions, never escalate.
    - Ephemeral Single-Use Seals: Consumable tokens invalidated upon first use, preventing replay attacks.

  OS Sandbox & Hardware Attestation (`std/src/ooda/sec/sys/landlock*.oo`, `std/src/ooda/sec/attest/`)
    - Linux Landlock LSM Sandboxing: Translates capability rights into kernel Landlock rulesets, restricting filesystem and network access directly inside the kernel.
    - POSIX Resource Limits & Cgroups v2 (`std/src/ooda/os/cgroup/`): Enforces hardware resource boundaries including `RLIMIT_AS`, `RLIMIT_CPU`, and Cgroups v2 `memory.max` / `cpu.weight`.
    - Hardware Attestation & TPM Quotes: Validates TPM 2.0 PCR banks, cryptographic quote signatures, and hardware platform identity.
    - Attested Monotonic Time: Hardware-derived timestamp verification guaranteeing bounded drift and monotonicity.
    - NIST SP 800-90B Continuous Entropy Testing: Real-time repetition count and adaptive proportion health checks on system entropy sources.

  Metamorphic Defense & ASLR Hardening (`std/src/ooda/sec/metamorphic/`)
    - METAMORPHIC: path-a: Randomized in-memory struct decoy padding and field offset diversification to thwart Return-Oriented Programming (ROP/JOP) attacks while preserving semantic field accessors.

================================================================================
3. Autonomous AI Agent Surface & Developer Tooling
================================================================================

  Agent-First Development Tools (`std/src/ooda/reflect/`, `std/src/ooda/fix/`)
    - Fast AST Signature Outlining (`ooda outline`): Extracts complete module signatures, function headers, struct definitions, and contract bounds without parsing implementation bodies, drastically reducing LLM token consumption.
    - Programmatic Docstring & DINNER Metadata Extraction (`ooda reflect`): Emits structured metadata and capability manifests for LLM agents.
    - Diagnostic Multi-Fix Engine (`ooda fix`): Translates type errors, missing capability tokens (`E_CAP`), and contract mismatches into unified, auto-applicable code diffs.
    - AST Metaprogramming & Macros (`std/src/ooda/macro/`, `oodac/ast_macros.oo`): Hygienic macro expansion engine with quasi-quoting (`QuoteNode`), syntax interpolation (`unquote`), and AST traversal.

  Language Server Protocol (LSP) Engine (`ooda/lsp/`, `std/src/ooda/lsp/`)
    - Native JSON-RPC 2.0 Server: High-throughput LSP engine with Content-Length framing.
    - Interactive IDE Diagnostics: Real-time publishDiagnostics, hover documentation resolution, and context-aware autocomplete suggestions.

  Automated Contract Fuzzing & Ghost State (`std/src/ooda/fuzz/`, `std/src/ooda/proofs/`)
    - Property-Based Contract Fuzzer: Automated input generator and mutation engine exploring integer, string, boolean, and compound boundaries against function contracts.
    - Idle Swarm Fuzz Daemon (`fuzz_net.oo`): Background fuzzing mesh executing during system idle periods to discover contract edge cases.
    - Transactional Ghost-State Verification: Pre-condition snapshotting and post-condition delta rollback for contracts.

================================================================================
4. Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) Governance & Audit Tracing
================================================================================

  Step-Pause Protocol & Authorization Gates (`std/src/ooda/hitl/`, `std/hitl.oo`)
    - Multi-Tier Approval Gates: Intercepts destructive actions (`is_destructive`) and external network/system effects (`is_external`), requiring explicit human authorization before side effects commit.
    - Strict Timeout Windows & Default-Deny: Enforces fail-closed evaluation where expired or unhandled requests automatically deny and abort.
    - Interactive HITL Step Loop: Session harness managing queued pause actions, operator approvals, and single-use execution tokens (`HitlToken`).
    - Cryptographic Audit Trail: Monotonically timestamped, tamper-evident audit record journal verifying operator identity, gate decisions, and action lifecycle.

================================================================================
5. In-Memory Merkle DAG & Time-Travel Undo RAM
================================================================================

  Cryptographic Merkle State Store (`std/src/ooda/merkle/`)
    - Binary Hash Tree Construction: SHA-256 leaf and intermediate node hashing creating immutable Merkle state roots.
    - Inclusion Proof Verification: Cryptographic audit path proofs verifying that a specific state frame belongs to a verified Merkle DAG snapshot.
    - Content-Addressable Directed Acyclic Graph: Immutable, deduplicated state storage with structural sharing.

  Time-Travel Undo RAM & Snapshot Engine (`std/src/ooda/undo/`, `std/undo.oo`)
    - High-Resolution In-Memory Ring Buffer: Cyclic snapshot logging recording scalar and byte-level memory delta frames (`DeltaFrame`) over execution time windows.
    - Instant Rollback Engine: Fast state restoration reverting modified memory state to previous snapshot checkpoints upon invariant failures, contract violations, or operator aborts.

================================================================================
6. Concurrency, Distributed Actors & Accelerated Compute
================================================================================

  Type-Safe Distributed Actor Framework (`std/src/ooda/actor/`)
    - Isolated Actor State & Bounded Mailboxes: Lock-free message passing with configurable mailbox capacities and backpressure policies.
    - Hierarchical Supervision Trees: Self-healing actor trees with `OneForOne` and `OneForAll` supervisor restart strategies and exponential backoff.
    - Flexible Message Routers: Round-robin, broadcast, and consistent hash routing strategies.

  Zero-Copy Concurrency Channels (`std/src/ooda/concurrency/`)
    - Ring Buffer Channels: High-throughput SPSC/MPMC lock-free ring buffers with cache-padded sequence counters.
    - Multi-Channel Select: Multiplexes non-blocking and blocking channel reads/writes.

  Data-Oriented Design (DoD) & Accelerated Compute (`std/src/ooda/dod/`, `std/src/ooda/gpu/`)
    - Struct-of-Arrays (SoA) Layouts: Columnar data representation with 64-byte CPU cache alignment.
    - SIMD Vector Pipelines: Streaming array transformations optimizing vector registers.
    - GPU / NPU Compute Kernels: Kernel dispatch pipelines gated by `&GpuCap` and `&NpuCap` capability tokens.
    - C-Header Importer & FFI Shims (`std/src/ooda/ffi/`, `std/ffi.oo`): Parses C headers (`typedef struct`, `extern fn`) and generates zero-cost OpenOODA capability-encased FFI wrappers.
    - Compiler Memory Telemetry (`std/src/ooda/perf/`, `std/perf.oo`): High-resolution `/proc/self/status` VmRSS/VmHWM sampler tracking compiler memory across phases (<8GB budget monitor).

================================================================================
7. Standard Library Ecosystem & Quality Standards
================================================================================

  Modular Standard Library (`std/` and `ooda/std/`)
    - Over 1,000 production modules covering Cryptography (SHA-256, HMAC, AES, Keccak), POSIX IO, Networking, 3D Graphics, Robotics, Quantum Simulation, Financial Calculations, and Enterprise Data.
    - 100% DINNER.oot 4-Element Academy Headers (`# Title`, `Logline:`, `Setup:`, `Beats:`).
    - 100% Modular Sizing Invariant: Every `.oo` file is strictly $\le 256$ lines (RULES.oot 1.7).
    - Automated Pre-Commit Enforcement: Git hooks and `dinner_lint.oo` validate formatting, sizing, and typechecks before commits land.

  Capability-Governed Package Manager (`ooda-pm`, `ooda/pm/`)
    - SemVer Constraint Solving: Caret (`^`), Tilde (`~`), and exact range resolution.
    - Zero-Trust Token Provenance: Capability Mint Authority (`std/src/ooda/sec/mint/`) validating token origin and monotonic rights attenuation.

================================================================================
8. Cryptographically Reproducible & Bit-Identical Build Attestation
================================================================================

  Canonical AST Serialization & Entropy Sanitizer (`std/src/ooda/repro/`, `std/repro.oo`)
    - Canonical AST Serializer: Eliminates filesystem ordering nondeterminism, strips source path leakages, and clamps timestamps against SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
    - Deterministic 256-bit Digest Generation: Calculates bit-identical canonical AST digests across compilation passes.
    - Multi-Compiler Attestation Validator: Ingests independent build seed attestations (GCC, Clang, WASM, LLVM), verifies bit-identical consensus, and issues tamper-evident certification.
    - Entropy Leak Detection: Automated scanning detecting and flagging leaked environment variables (HOSTNAME, USER, BUILD_TIMESTAMP).

================================================================================
9. Live Process Code Hot-Swapping & Dynamic State Schema Migration
================================================================================

  Hot-Swap & Schema Evolution Engine (`std/src/ooda/hotswap/`, `std/hotswap.oo`)
    - Live Symbol Patching: Relocates and updates module function symbol tables in running processes without restart, gated by `&HotswapCap`.
    - Dynamic State Migration: Transforms live in-memory data structures across schema versions v(N) to v(N+1) with automatic field defaulting and custom migration handlers.
    - Atomic Transactional Rollback: Safeguards hot-swap sessions by automatically reverting live symbol pointers and restoring previous state buffers if migration faults occur.

================================================================================
10. Field-Level Information Flow Taint Tracking & Secret Sink Guards
================================================================================

  Information Flow Control & Leak Prevention (`std/src/ooda/sec/taint/`, `std/taint.oo`)
    - Inter-Procedural Taint Lattice: Tracks and joins sensitivity labels (`SECRET`, `USER_INPUT`, `UNTRUSTED_NET`) across variable assignments, expressions, and struct field projections.
    - Sink Guard Verification: Enforces strict compile-time and runtime checks preventing tainted data from reaching unauthorized sinks (`LogSink`, `NetEgressSink`, `FsWriteSink`, `ExecSink`).
    - Cryptographic Sanitizer Enforcement: Requires verified declassification and hashing sanitizers before high-sensitivity data can be emitted.

================================================================================
11. Pause-Free Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR) & Zero-Fragmentation Slab Arenas
================================================================================

  Concurrent Memory Management (`std/src/ooda/mm/`, `std/mm.oo`)
    - Lock-Free Epoch-Based Reclamation: Manages concurrent memory life cycles across global epochs with zero stop-the-world garbage collection pauses.
    - Thread-Pinned Safe Reclamation: Defers node deallocations until all threads progress past the retiring epoch, eliminating use-after-free conditions.
    - Zero-Fragmentation Slab Arena Pools: Pre-allocated memory slabs delivering O(1) allocation velocity and SIMD 64-byte aligned memory chunks with 0 ppm external fragmentation.

================================================================================
Sidecars & Tooling
================================================================================
  - VS Code Integration: `vscode/` language client with real-time `ooda-lsp` diagnostics and hover info.
  - Tree-Sitter Grammar: `tree-sitter/` full grammar specification for syntax highlighting.
  - Runtime Hide: `ooda/runtime/oo_hide.c` 16-slot load-time table.
  - Hologram Persistence: `ooda/runtime/oo_holo.c` content-addressed persistent blob engine.
